    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.107 WN16-CC-000160"
      info        : "Downloading print driver packages over HTTP must be prevented.

GROUP ID:V-224926
RULE ID:SV-224926r958478

Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and will prevent uncontrolled updates to the system.

This setting prevents the computer from downloading print driver packages over HTTP."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> System >> Internet Communication Management >> Internet Communication settings >> \'Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP\'

to \'Enabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-224926r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN16-CC-000160,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23093"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Nt\Printers"
      reg_item    : "DisableWebPnPDownload"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.108 WN16-CC-000170"
      info        : "Printing over HTTP must be prevented.

GROUP ID:V-224927
RULE ID:SV-224927r958478

Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and will prevent uncontrolled updates to the system.

This setting prevents the client computer from printing over HTTP, which allows the computer to print to printers on the intranet as well as the Internet."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> System >> Internet Communication Management >> Internet Communication settings >> \'Turn off printing over HTTP\'

to \'Enabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-224927r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN16-CC-000170,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23093"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Nt\Printers"
      reg_item    : "DisableHTTPPrinting"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
