    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.121 WN16-CC-000330"
      info        : "Windows Server 2016 Windows SmartScreen must be enabled.

GROUP ID: V-224940
RULE ID: SV-224940r958478

Windows SmartScreen helps protect systems from programs downloaded from the internet that may be malicious. Enabling SmartScreen will warn users of potentially malicious programs."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> File Explorer >> \'Configure Windows SmartScreen\' to \'Enabled\''
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-224940r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN16-CC-000330,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-224940"
