      powershell_args : "Get-WindowsFeature | Where {$_.Name -eq 'FS-SMB1'} | SELECT 'InstallState' | Format-List"
      check_type      : CHECK_NOT_REGEX
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.39 WN16-00-000411"
      info        : "The Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol must be disabled on the SMB server.

GROUP ID:V-224857
RULE ID:SV-224857r958478

SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> MS Security Guide >> \'Configure SMBv1 Server\' to \'Disabled\'

The system must be restarted for the change to take effect.

This policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \'SecGuide.admx\' and \'SecGuide.adml\' must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-224857r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN16-00-000411,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-73299"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23093"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "0"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\System\Currentcontrolset\Services\Lanmanserver\Parameters"
      reg_item    : "SMB1"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "Check if no accounts are members of the Backup Operators group."
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "PASS: No accounts are part of the Backup Operators group."
          powershell_args : '$group=\\"Backup Operators\\"; $members=Get-LocalGroupMember -Group $group -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; if ($members) { Write-Host "WARNING: \\\'$group\\\' group has members: "; $members | ForEach-Object { Write-Host $_.Name } } else { Write-Host "PASS: No accounts are part of the "$group" group." }'
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.4 WN16-00-000050"
          info        : "Members of the Backup Operators group must have separate accounts for backup duties and normal operational tasks.

GROUP ID:V-224822
RULE ID:SV-224822r991589

Backup Operators are able to read and write to any file in the system, regardless of the rights assigned to it. Backup and restore rights permit users to circumvent the file access restrictions present on NTFS disk drives for backup and restore purposes. Members of the Backup Operators group must have separate logon accounts for performing backup duties."
          solution    : "Ensure each member of the Backup Operators group has separate accounts for backup functions and standard user functions."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-224822r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN16-00-000050,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23093"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.4 WN16-00-000050"
